## Endpoints

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `/` | Service identity |
| `/healthz` | Liveness: the process is up |
| `/readyz` | Readiness: the process can serve traffic |
| `/metrics` | Prometheus metrics |

`/healthz` and `/readyz` answer different questions on purpose. Liveness must
never depend on anything external, or an outage in a dependency turns into a
restart loop; readiness is where "cannot serve right now" belongs.

## No dependencies

This service uses the standard library only. The metrics endpoint writes
Prometheus exposition format by hand, which is about sixty lines for a counter
and a duration total — cheaper than a dependency, a `go.sum` to keep in sync and
a supply chain to audit. Reach for `prometheus/client_golang` the day the metrics
stop being trivial.

